	Of Hezron: the family of the Hezronites. Of Carmi: the
	family of the Carmites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the Reubenites, and their counts
	were forty-three thousand seven hundred thirty.
}

\eR{
	And Eliab’s sons: Nemuel and Dathan and Abiram. That is
	the Dathan and Abiram, prominent ones of the congregation,
	who fought against Moses and against Aaron in Korah’s
	congregation when they fought against YHWH,%
}

\eR{
	and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them and
	Korah when the congregation died, when the fire consumed
	the two hundred fifty men, and they became a sign.%
}

\eP{
	The children of Simeon by their families: Of Nemuel: the
	family of the Nemuelites. Of Jamin: the family of the
	Jaminites. Of Jachin: the family of the Jachinites.
}

\eP{
	Of Zerah: the family of the Zerahites. Of Saul: the family
	of the Saulites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the Simeonites: twenty-two
	thousand two hundred.
}

\eP{
	The children of Gad by their families: Of Zephon: the
	family of the Zephonites. Of Haggi: the family of the
	Haggites. Of Shuni: the family of the Shunites.
}

\eP{
	Of Ozni: the family of the Oznites. Of Eri: the family of
	the Erites.
}

\eP{
	Of Arod: the family of the Arodites. Of Areli: the family
	of the Arelites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the children of Gad by their
	counts: forty thousand five hundred.
}

\eP{
	Judah’s sons were Er and Onan, but Er and Onan died in the
	land of Canaan.
}

\eP{
	Then the children of Judah by their families were: Of
	Shelah: the family of the Shelanites. Of Perez: the family
	of the Perezites. Of Zerah: the family of the Zerahites.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Perez were: Of Hezron: the family of
	the Hezronites. Of Hamul: the family of the Hamulites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of Judah by their counts:
	seventy-six thousand five hundred.
}

\eP{
	The children of Issachar by their families: Tola: the
	family of the Tolaites. Of Puwah, the family of the
	Punites.
}

\eP{
	Of Jashub: the family of the Jashubites. Of Shimron: the
	family of the Shimronites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of Issachar by their counts:
	sixty-four thousand three hundred.
}

\eP{
	The children of Zebulun by their families: Of Sered: the
	family of the Seredites. Of Elon: the family of the
	Elonites. Of Jahleel: the family of the Jahleelites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the Zebulunites by their counts:
	sixty thousand five hundred.
}

\eP{
	The children of Joseph by their families were Manasseh and
	Ephraim.
}

\eP{
	Of the children of Manasseh: Of Machir: the family of the
	Machirites. And Machir fathered Gilead. Of Gilead: the
	family of the Gileadites.
}

\eP{
	These are the children of Gilead: Of Iezer: the family of
	the Iezerites. Of Helek: the family of the Helekites.
}

\eP{
	And Asriel: the family of the Asrielites. And Shechem: the
	family of the Shechemites.
}

\eP{
	And Shemida: the family of the Shemidaites. And Hepher:
	the family of the Hepherites.
}

\eP{
	And Zelophehad son of Hepher had no sons, just daughters,
	and the names of Zelophehad’s daughters were Mahlah and
	Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of Manasseh; and their counts:
	fifty-two thousand seven hundred.
}

\eP{
	These are the children of Ephraim by their families: Of
	Shuthelah: the family of the Shuthelahites. Of Becher: the
	family of the Becherites. Of Tahan: the family of the
	Tahanites.
}

\eP{
	And these are the children of Shuthelah: Of Eran: the
	family of the Eranites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the children of Ephraim by their
	counts: thirty-two thousand five hundred. These are the
	sons of Joseph after their families.
}

\eP{
	The children of Benjamin by their families: Of Bela: the
	family of the Belaites. Of Ashbel: the family of the
	Ashbelites. Of Ahiram: the family of the Ahiramites.
}

\eP{
	Of Shephupham: the family of the Shuphamites. Of Hupham:
	the family of the Huphamites.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Bela were Ard and Naaman: the family
	of the Ardites. Of Naaman: the family of the Naamites.
}

\eP{
	These are the children of Benjamin by their families; and
	their counts: forty-five thousand six hundred.
}

\eP{
	These are the children of Dan by their families: Of
	Shuham: the family of the Shuhamites. These are the
	families of Dan after their families.
}

\eP{
	All the families of the Shuhamites by their counts:
	sixty-four thousand four hundred.
}

\eP{
	The children of Asher by their families: Of Imnah: the
	family of Imnah. Of Ishvi: the family of the Ishvites. Of
	Beriah: the family of the Beriites.
}

\eP{
	Of the children of Beriah: Of Heber: the family of the
	Heberites. Of Malchiel: the family of the Malchielites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the children of Asher by their
	counts: fifty-three thousand four hundred.
}

\eP{
	The children of Naphtali by their families: Of Jahzeel:
	the family of the Jahzeelites. Of Guni: the family of the
	Gunites.
}

\eP{
	Of Jezer: the family of the Jezerites. Of Shillem: the
	family of the Shillemites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of Naphtali by their families, and
	their counts: forty-five thousand four hundred.
}

\eP{
	These are the counts of the children of Israel: six
	hundred one thousand seven hundred thirty.
}

\eP{
	“The land shall be distributed to these as a legacy with
	the number of names.
}

\eP{
	For the large you shall make its legacy larger, and for
	the small you shall make its legacy smaller. Each man will
	be given his legacy according to his counts.
}

\eP{
	Just: the land shall be distributed by lot. They shall
	have a legacy by the names of their fathers’ tribes.
}

\eP{
	Its legacy shall be distributed according to the lot,
	whether large or small.”
}

\eP{
	And these are the counts of the Levites by their families:
	Of Gershon: the family of the Gershonites. Of Kohath: the
	family of the Kohathites. Of Merari: the family of the
	Merarites.
}

\eP{
	These are the families of the Levites: the family of the
	Libnites, the family of the Hebronites, the family of the
	Mahlites, the family of the Mushites, the family of the
	Korahites. And Kohath fathered Amram.
}

\eP{
	And the name of Amram’s wife was Jochebed, a daughter of
	Levi, who was born to Levi in Egypt. And she gave birth
	for Amram to Aaron and Moses and Miriam, their sister.
}

\eP{
	And Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar were born to
	Aaron.
}

\eP{
	And Nadab and Abihu died when they brought forward
	unfitting fire in front of YHWH.
}

\eP{
	And their counts were twenty-three thousand, every male
	from a month old and up, because they were not counted
	among the children of Israel because a legacy was not
	given to them among the children of Israel.
}

\eP{
	These are the counts of Moses and Eleazar, the priest, who
	counted the children of Israel in the plains of Moab by
	the Jordan toward Jericho;
}

\eP{
	and there was not a man among these from the counts of
	Moses and Aaron, the priest, who counted the children of
	Israel in the wilderness of Sinai,
}

\eP{
	because YHWH said of them, “They shall die in the
	wilderness,” and not a man was left of them except Caleb
	son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun.
}

\eP{
	And they stood in front of Moses and in front of Eleazar,
	the priest, and in front of the chieftains and all the
	congregation at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting,
	saying,
}

\eP{
	“Our father died in the wilderness. And he wasn’t among
	the congregation who were gathered against YHWH: in
	Korah’s congregation. Rather, he died through his own sin.
	And he had no sons.
}

\eP{
	Why should our father’s name be subtracted from among his
	family because he didn’t have a son? Give us a possession
	among our father’s brothers.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses brought their case forward in front of YHWH.
}

\eP{
	“Zelophehad’s daughters speak right. You shall give them a
	possession for a legacy among their father’s brothers, and
	you shall pass their father’s legacy to them.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		Zelophehad’s daughters speak right. See the comment on Num 36:5.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	And you shall speak to the children of Israel, saying, ‘A
	man who will die and not have a son: you shall pass his
	legacy to his daughter.
}

\eP{
	And if he does not have a daughter, then you shall give
	his legacy to his brothers.
}

\eP{
	And if he does not have brothers, then you shall give his
	legacy to his father’s brothers.
}

\eP{
	And YHWH said to Moses, “Go up to this mountain of Abarim
	and see the land that I’ve given to the children of
	Israel.
}

\eP{
	And you’ll see it, and then you’ll be gathered to your
	people, you as well, as Aaron, your brother, was gathered,
}

\eP{
	because you rebelled against my word in the wilderness of
	Zin in the congregation’s quarrel to make me holy with
	water before their eyes. That is the water of Meribah of
	Kadesh at the wilderness of Zin.”
}

\eP{
	“Let YHWH, God of the spirits of all flesh, appoint a man
	over the congregation
}

\eP{
	who will go out in front of them and who will come in in
	front of them and who will bring them out and who will
	bring them in, so YHWH’s congregation won’t be like sheep
	that don’t have a shepherd.”
}

\eP{
	And YHWH said to Moses, “Take Joshua son of Nun, a man
	with spirit in him, and lay your hand on him.
}

\eP{
	And you shall stand him in front of Eleazar, the priest,
	and in front of all the congregation, and you shall
	command him before their eyes.
}

\eP{
	And you shall put some of your eminence on him so that all
	the congregation of the children of Israel will hear.
}

\eP{
	And Moses did as YHWH commanded him, and he took Joshua
	and stood him in front of Eleazar, the priest, and in
	front of all the congregation.
}

\eP{
	And he laid his hands on him and commanded him, as YHWH
	had spoken by Moses’ hand.
}

\eR{
	“Command the children of Israel, and you shall say to
	them: You shall observe to bring forward my sacrifice to
	me, my bread, for my offering by fire, my pleasant smell,
	at its appointed time.%
}

\eR{
	“And you shall say to them: This is the offering by fire
	that you shall bring forward to YHWH: two unblemished
	one-year-old lambs per day as a continual burnt offering.%
}

\eR{
	You shall do one lamb in the morning, and you shall do the
	second lamb ‘between the two evenings.’%
}

\eR{
	And a tenth of an ephah of fine flour for a grain
	offering, mixed with a fourth of a hin of pressed oil,%
}

\eR{
	the continual burnt offering that was done at Mount Sinai
	for a pleasant smell, an offering by fire to YHWH.%
}

\eR{
	And its libation shall be a fourth of a hin for one lamb.
	Pour a libation of beer in the holy place for YHWH.%
}

\eR{
	And you shall do the second lamb ‘between the two
	evenings,’ and you shall do it like the morning grain
	offering and like its libation, an offering by fire of a
	pleasant smell to YHWH.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the Sabbath day two unblemished one-year-old lambs
	and two tenths of fine flour, a grain offering, mixed with
	oil, and its libation:%
}

\eR{
	the burnt offering of each Sabbath in its week, beside the
	continual burnt offering and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“And at the beginning of your months you shall bring
	forward a burnt offering to YHWH: two bulls of the cattle
	and one ram, seven unblemished one-year-old lambs,%
}

\eR{
	with three tenths of fine flour, a grain offering, mixed
	with oil for one bull and two tenths of fine flour mixed
	with oil for the one ram,%
}

\eR{
	and one tenth of fine flour, a grain offering, mixed with
	oil for each lamb, a burnt offering as a pleasant smell,
	an offering by fire to YHWH.%
}

\eR{
	And their libations: half a hin will be for a bull and a
	third of a hin for a ram and a fourth of a hin for a
	lamb—wine. This is the burnt offering of each new month in
	its month for the months of the year.%
}

\eR{
	And one goat for a sin offering to YHWH shall be done,
	beside the continual burnt offering and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“And in the first month on the fourteenth day of the month
	is a Passover to YHWH.%
}

\eR{
	And on the fifteenth day of this month is a holiday. For
	seven days unleavened bread shall be eaten.%
}

\eR{
	On the first day is a holy assembly. You shall not do any
	act of work.%
}

\eR{
	And you shall bring forward an offering by fire, a burnt
	offering to YHWH. You shall have two bulls of the cattle
	and one ram and seven unblemished one-year-old lambs.%
}

\eR{
	And their grain offering shall be fine flour mixed with
	oil. You shall do three tenths for a bull and two tenths
	for a ram.%
}

\eR{
	And you shall do one tenth for each lamb, for the seven
	lambs.%
}

\eR{
	And one goat for a sin offering to make atonement over
	you.%
}

\eR{
	You shall do these aside from the morning burnt offering
	that is for the continual burnt offering.%
}

\eR{
	You shall do food as a fire offering, a pleasant smell to
	YHWH, like these daily for seven days. It shall be done
	beside the continual burnt offering and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	And on the seventh day you shall have a holy assembly. You
	shall not do any act of work.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the Day of Firstfruits, when you bring a new grain
	offering to YHWH on your Feast of Weeks, you shall have a
	holy assembly. You shall not do any act of work.%
}

\eR{
	And you shall bring forward a burnt offering for a
	plea-sant smell to YHWH: two bulls of the cattle, one ram,
	seven one-year-old lambs%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering, fine flour mixed with oil, three
	tenths for one bull, two tenths for one ram,%
}

\eR{
	You shall do it aside from the continual burnt offering
	and its grain offering—they shall be unblemished for
	you—and their libations.%
}

\eR{
	“And in the seventh month on the first of the month you
	shall have a holy assembly. You shall not do any act of
	work. You shall have a day of horn-blasting.%
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		seventh month on the first of the month. This is the holiday that later
%		came to be known as Rosh Hashanah, the New Year. It is never called by
%		that name in the Torah, where it is rather counted as the seventh month.
%	}

tex.english:
\eR{
	And you shall do a burnt offering for a pleasant smell for
	YHWH: one bull of the cattle, one ram, seven unblemished
	one-year-old lambs,%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering, fine flour mixed with oil, three
	tenths for a bull, two tenths for a ram,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering to make atonement over
	you,%
}

\eR{
	aside from the burnt offering of the new month and its
	grain offering and the continual burnt offering and its
	grain offering and their libations as required, for a
	pleasant smell, an offering by fire to YHWH.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the tenth of this seventh month you shall have a
	holy assembly. And you shall degrade yourselves. You shall
	not do any act of work.%
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		on the tenth of this seventh month. This is the Day of Atonement, Yom
%		Kippur.
%	}

tex.english:
\eR{
	And you shall bring forward a burnt offering to YHWH for a
	pleasant smell: you shall have one bull of the cattle, one
	ram, seven unblemished one-year-old lambs,%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering, fine flour mixed with oil, three
	tenths for a bull, two tenths for one ram,%
}

\eR{
	one goat for a sin offering, aside from the sin offering
	of atonement and the continual burnt offering and its
	grain offering and their libations.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the fifteenth day of the seventh month you shall
	have a holy assembly. You shall not do any act of work.
	And you shall celebrate a holiday for YHWH for seven days.%
}

\eR{
	And you shall bring forward a burnt offering, an offering
	by fire for a pleasant smell to YHWH: thirteen bulls of
	the cattle, two rams, fourteen one-year-old lambs. They
	shall be unblemished.%
}

\eR{
	And their grain offering shall be fine flour mixed with
	oil, three tenths for each bull, for thirteen bulls, two
	tenths for each ram, for two rams,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering, its grain offering, and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the second day: twelve bulls of the cattle, two
	rams, fourteen unblemished one-year-old lambs%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering and their libations for the
	bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs by their number as
	required,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering and its grain offering and their libations.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the third day: eleven bulls, two rams, fourteen
	unblemished one-year-old lambs%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering and their libations for the
	bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs by their number as
	required,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering and its grain offering and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the fourth day: ten bulls, two rams, fourteen
	unblemished one-year-old lambs,%
}

\eR{
	their grain offering and their libations for the bulls,
	for the rams, and for the lambs by their number as
	required,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering, its grain offering, and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the fifth day: nine bulls, two rams, fourteen
	unblemished one-year-old lambs%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering and their libations for the
	bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs by their number as
	required,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering and its grain offering and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the sixth day: eight bulls, two rams, fourteen
	unblemished one-year-old lambs%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering and their libations for the
	bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs by their number as
	required,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering, its grain offering, and its libations.%
}

\eR{
	“And on the seventh day: seven bulls, two rams, fourteen
	unblemished one-year-old lambs%
}

\eR{
	and their grain offering and their libations for the
	bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs by their number
	according to their requirement,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering, its grain offering, and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“On the eighth day you shall have a convocation. You shall
	not do any act of work.%
}

\eR{
	And you shall bring forward a burnt offering, an offering
	by fire, a pleasant smell to YHWH: one bull, one ram,
	seven unblemished one-year-old lambs,%
}

\eR{
	their grain offering and their libations for the bull, for
	the ram, and for the lambs by their number as required,%
}

\eR{
	and one goat for a sin offering, aside from the continual
	burnt offering and its grain offering and its libation.%
}

\eR{
	“You shall do these for YHWH at your appointed times,
	aside from your vows and your contributions for your burnt
	offerings and for your grain offerings and for your
	libations and for your peace offerings.”%
}

\eP{
	And Moses said it to the children of Israel, according
	to everything that YHWH commanded Moses.
}

\eP{
	And Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes of the
	children of Israel, saying, “This is the thing that YHWH
	commanded:
}

\eP{
	A man who will make a vow to YHWH or has sworn an oath to
	make a restriction on himself shall not desecrate his
	word. He shall do it according to everything that comes
	out of his mouth.
}

\eP{
	“And a woman who will make a vow to YHWH and made a
	restriction in her father’s house in her youth,
}

\eP{
	and her father hears her vow and her restriction that she
	made on herself, and her father keeps quiet to her, then
	all her vows shall stand, and every restriction that she
	made on herself shall stand.
}

\eP{
	But if her father held her back on the day he heard all
	her vows and her restrictions that she made on herself, it
	will not stand. And YHWH will forgive her because her
	father held her back.
}

\eP{
	“And if she will have a husband while her vows or the
	thing she let out of her lips with which she restricted
	herself are on her,
}

\eP{
	and her husband hears and keeps quiet on the day he heard
	it, then her vows will stand, and her restrictions that
	she made on herself will stand.
}

\eP{
	But if, on the day her husband hears it, he will hold her
	back and will break her vow that is on her and what was
	let out of her lips by which she restricted herself, then
	YHWH will forgive her.
}

\eP{
	“And a widow’s or divorced woman’s vow, everything by
	which she has restricted herself, shall stand regarding
	her.
}

\eP{
	“And if she vowed or made a restriction on herself by an
	oath at her husband’s house,
}

\eP{
	and her husband heard it and kept quiet to her—he did not
	hold her back—then all her vows shall stand, and every
	restriction that she made on herself shall stand.
}

\eP{
	But if her husband broke them on the day he heard all that
	came out of her lips for her vows and for restricting
	herself, it shall not stand. Her husband had broken them,
	and YHWH will forgive her.
}

\eP{
	Every vow and every oath of restriction to degrade
	oneself: her husband shall make it stand, and her husband
	shall break it.
}

\eP{
	And if he will break them after he has heard them, then he
	shall bear her crime.”
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		he shall bear her crime. Having power over another person also means
%		taking responsibility for that person’s actions. If a man causes his
%		wife to violate a vow she made, then it is he who must live with the
%		consequences.
%	}

tex.english:
\eOther{
	These are the laws that YHWH commanded Moses between a man
	and his wife, between a father and his daughter in her
	youth at her father’s house.
}

\eP{
	“Get revenge for the children of Israel from the
	Midianites. After that you’ll be gathered to your people.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses spoke to the people, saying, “Let people from
	you be equipped for the army, so they’ll be against Midian
	to put YHWH’s revenge in Midian.
}

\eP{
	You shall send a thousand per tribe, a thousand per tribe,
	for all Israel’s tribes, to the army.”
}

\eP{
	And, from Israel’s thousands, a thousand per tribe were
	delivered, twelve thousand equipped for the army.
}

\eP{
	And Moses sent them, a thousand per tribe, to the army;
	them and Phinehas son of Eleazar, the priest, to the army,
	with the equipment of the Holy and the trumpets for
	blasting in his hand.
}

\eP{
	And they made war on Midian as YHWH had commanded Moses.
	And they killed every male.
}

\eP{
	And they killed the kings of Midian—Evi and Rekem and Zur
	and Hur and Reba, the five kings of Midian—over their
	corpses. And they killed Balaam son of Beor by the sword.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Israel took the women of Midian and
	their infants prisoner, and they despoiled all their
	animals and all their livestock and all their wealth.
}

\eP{
	And they burned all their cities with their homes and all
	their encampments in fire.
}

\eP{
	And they took all the spoil and all the prey, human and
	animal.
}

\eP{
	And they brought the prisoners and the prey and the spoil
	to Moses and to Eleazar, the priest, and to the
	congregation of the children of Israel, to the camp, to
	the plains of Moab, which is by the Jordan toward Jericho.
}

\eP{
	And Moses and Eleazar, the priest, and all the
	congregation’s chieftains went out to them, outside the
	camp.
}

\eP{
	And Moses was angry at the officers of the army, the
	chiefs of thousands and the chiefs of hundreds who were
	coming from the army of the war.
}

\eP{
	Here, they came to bring about a breach against YHWH by
	the children of Israel, at Balaam’s word, over the matter
	of Peor, so there was the plague in YHWH’s congregation!
}

\eP{
	So now, kill every male among the infants, and kill every
	woman who has known a man for male intercourse.
}

\eP{
	But all infants among the women who have not known a
	male’s inter-course: keep alive.
}

\eP{
	And you, camp outside the camp for seven days: everyone
	who killed a life and everyone who touched a corpse, do
	sin expiation on the third day and on the seventh day, you
	and your prisoners.
}

\eP{
	And for every piece of clothing and every leather item and
	everything made from goats and every wood item you shall
	do expiation.”
}

\eP{
	And Eleazar, the priest, said to the men of the army who
	had come to the war, “This is the law of the instruction
	that YHWH commanded Moses:
}

\eP{
	Just the gold and the silver, the bronze, the iron, the
	tin, and the lead,
}

\eP{
	every thing that will go in fire, you shall pass through
	fire and purify. It shall be expiated from sin just in
	water of impurity. And everything that will not go in
	fire, you shall pass through water.
}

\eP{
	And you shall wash your clothes on the seventh day, and
	you will be pure, and after that you shall come to the
	camp.”
}

\eP{
	“Add up the heads of the prey, the prisoners, human and
	animal, you and Eleazar, the priest, and the heads of the
	fathers of the congregation.
}

\eP{
	And you shall split the prey between the warriors who went
	out to the army and all the congregation.
}

\eP{
	And you shall levy a tax for YHWH from the men of war who
	went out to the army, one individual out of five hundred,
	from humans and from cattle and from asses and from sheep.
}

\eP{
	You shall take from their half and you shall give to
	Eleazar, the priest, YHWH’s donation.
}

\eP{
	And Moses and Eleazar, the priest, did as YHWH commanded
	Moses.
}

\eP{
	And the prey, over and above the spoil that the people of
	the army had taken, was: six hundred seventy-five thousand
	sheep
}

\eP{
	and human beings—from the women who had not known male
	intercourse—all the persons were thirty-two thousand.
}

\eP{
	So the half, the portion of those who went out in the army
	was: the number of sheep was three hundred thirty-seven
	thousand five hundred.
}

\eP{
	And the tax for YHWH from the sheep was six hundred
	seventy-five.
}

\eP{
	And the cattle were thirty-six thousand, and their tax for
	YHWH was seventy-two.
}

\eP{
	And asses were thirty thousand five hundred, and their tax
	for YHWH was sixty-one.
}

\eP{
	And human beings were sixteen thousand, and their tax for
	YHWH was thirty-two persons.
}

\eP{
	And Moses gave the tax, a donation for YHWH, to Eleazar,
	the priest, as YHWH commanded Moses.
}

\eP{
	And of the half for the children of Israel, which Moses
	had split from the people who were serving in the army:
}

\eP{
	and the congregation’s half of the sheep was three hundred
	thirty-seven thousand five hundred.
}

\eP{
	And Moses took from the half of the children of Israel one
	share out of fifty, from humans and from animals, and gave
	them to the Levites, who kept the watch of YHWH’s
	Tabernacle, as YHWH commanded Moses.
}

\eP{
	And the officers who were over the thousands of the army
	came forward to Moses, the chiefs of the thousands and the
	chiefs of the hundreds.
}

\eP{
	And they said to Moses, “Your servants have added up the
	heads of the men of war who are in our hands, and not a
	man of them is lacking.
}

\eP{
	And we have made an offering for YHWH—whatever each man
	found: an item of gold, an armlet or bracelet, a ring, an
	earring, or an ornament—to make atonement for ourselves in
	front of YHWH.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses and Eleazar, the priest, took the gold from
	them, every item of handiwork.
}

\eP{
	And all the gold of the donation that they donated to YHWH
	was sixteen thousand seven hundred fifty shekels, from the
	chiefs of the thousands and from the chiefs of the
	hundreds.
}

\eP{
	And Moses and Eleazar, the priest, took the gold from the
	chiefs of the thousands and the hundreds and brought it to
	the Tent of Meeting, a commemoration for the children of
	Israel in front of YHWH.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Reuben and the children of Gad had
	a great amount of livestock, very substantial. And they
	saw the land of Jazer and the land of Gilead, and here:
	the place was a place for livestock.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Gad and the children of Reuben came
	and said to Moses and to Eleazar, the priest, and to the
	chieftains of the congregation, saying,
}

\eP{
	“Ataroth and Dibon and Jazer and Nimrah and Heshbon and
	Elealeh and Sebam and Nebo and Beon,
}

\eP{
	the land that YHWH struck in front of the congregation of
	Israel: it’s livestock land, and your servants have
	livestock.”
}

\eP{
	And they said, “If we’ve found favor in your eyes, let
	this land be given to your servants for a possession.
	Don’t have us cross the Jordan.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses said to the children of Gad and to the children
	of Reuben, “Will your brothers go to war while you sit
	here?!
}

\eP{
	And why do you hold back the heart of the children of
	Israel from crossing to the land that YHWH has given them?
}

\eP{
	That’s what your fathers did when I sent them from
	Kadesh-barnea to see the land.
}

\eP{
	And they went up to the Wadi Eshcol and saw the land, but
	they held back the heart of the children of Israel so as
	not to go to the land that YHWH had given them.
}

\eP{
	‘The people who came up from Egypt, from twenty years old
	and up, won’t see the land that I swore to Abraham, to
	Isaac, and to Jacob, because they didn’t go after me
	completely,
}

\eP{
	except Caleb son of Jephunneh, the Kenizzite, and Joshua
	son of Nun because they went after YHWH completely.’
}

\eP{
	And YHWH’s anger flared at Israel, and he made them roam
	in the wilderness forty years, until the end of all the
	generation who were doing bad in YHWH’s eyes.
}

\eP{
	And, here, you’ve gotten up in your fathers’ place, a
	group of sinning people, to add more onto YHWH’s flaring
	anger at Israel.
}

\eP{
	If you go back from behind Him, then He’ll add more to
	leave them in the wilderness, and you’ll have destroyed
	all of this people!”
}

\eP{
	And they came over to him and said, “We’ll build walls for
	our livestock here, and cities for our infants.
}

\eP{
	And we shall be equipped, ready in front of the children
	of Israel until we’ve brought them to their place, and our
	infants will live in fortified cities because of the
	residents of the land.
}

\eP{
	We won’t go back to our houses until the children of
	Israel take possession, each of his legacy.
}

\eP{
	Because we won’t have a possession with them from the
	farther side of the Jordan, because our possession has
	come to us from the eastward side of the Jordan.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses said to them, “If you’ll do this thing: if
	you’ll get equipped for war in front of YHWH,
}

\eP{
	and every one of you will cross the Jordan equipped in
	front of YHWH until He dispossesses his enemies in front
	of him,
}

\eP{
	and the land will be subdued in front of YHWH, then, after
	that, you’ll go back, and, from YHWH and from Israel,
	you’ll be free, and this land will become yours for a
	possession in front of YHWH.
}

\eP{
	But if you won’t do this, here, you’ve sinned to YHWH, and
	know that your sin will find you.
}

\eP{
	Build cities for your infants and fences for your flocks,
	and do what has come out of your mouths.”
}

\eP{
	And the children of Gad and the children of Reuben said to
	Moses, saying, “Your servants will do as my lord commands.
}

\eP{
	Our infants, our women, our livestock, and all our animals
	will be there in the cities of Gilead.
}

\eP{
	And your servants will cross, everyone equipped for the
	army, in front of YHWH for war as my lord speaks.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses commanded Eleazar, the priest, and Joshua son of
	Nun and the heads of the fathers of the tribes of the
	children of Israel for them.
}

\eP{
	But if they will not cross equipped with you, then they
	will have possessions among you in the land of Canaan.”
}

\eP{
	And the children of Gad and the children of Reuben
	answered, saying, “What YHWH has spoken to your servants:
	we shall do so.
}

\eP{
	We’ll cross equipped in front of YHWH to the land of
	Canaan while we’ll have our legacy possession across the
	Jordan.”
}

\eP{
	and Beth-Nimrah and Beth-Haran, fortified cities and
	fences for flocks.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Reuben built Heshbon and Elealeh and
	Kiriathaim
}

\eP{
	and Nebo and Baal-meon—with changes of name—and Sibmah,
	and they called the names of the cities that they built by
	new names.
}

\eP{
	And the children of Machir son of Manasseh went to Gilead
	and captured it and dispossessed the Amorite who was in
	it.
}

\eP{
	And Moses gave Gilead to Machir son of Manasseh, and they
	lived in it.
}

\eP{
	And Jair son of Manasseh went and captured their villages,
	and he called them Havvoth-Jair.
}

\eP{
	And Nobah went and captured Kenath and its towns, and he
	called it Nobah after his own name.
}

\eOther{
	These are the travels of the children of Israel who went
	out from the land of Egypt by their armies
}
\eR{by the hand of Moses and Aaron.}

\eR{
	And Moses wrote their stops for their travels by YHWH’s
	word, and these are their travels and their stops.%
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Rameses in the first month on the
	fifteenth day of the first month. On the day after the
	Passover, the children of Israel went out with a high hand
	before the eyes of all Egypt.
}

\eOther{
	And the Egyptians were burying those whom YHWH had struck
	among them: every firstborn. And YHWH had made judgments
	on their gods.
}

\eOther{
	And the children of Israel traveled from Rameses and
	camped in Succoth.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Succoth and camped in Etham, which
	is at the edge of the wilderness.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Etham and turned back toward
	Pi-hahiroth, which is in front of Baal-Zephon: and they
	camped in front of Migdol.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from before Pi-hahiroth and passed
	through the sea to the wilderness. And they went three
	days’ journey in the wilderness of Etham and camped in
	Marah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Marah and came to Elim. And in Elim
	were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees. And
	they camped there.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Elim and camped by the Red Sea.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from the Red Sea and camped in the
	wilderness of Sin.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from the wilderness of Sin and camped in
	Dophkah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Dophkah and camped in Alush.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Alush and camped at Rephidim. And
	there was no water there for the people to drink.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Rephidim and camped in the
	wilderness of Sinai.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from the wilderness of Sinai and camped
	at Kibroth Hattaavah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Kibroth Hattaavah and camped at
	Hazeroth.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Hazeroth and camped in Rithmah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Rithmah and camped at Rimmon-parez.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Rimmon-parez and camped in Libnah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Libnah and camped at Rissah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Rissah and camped in Kehelathah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Kehelathah and camped at Mount
	Shapher.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Mount Shapher and camped in
	Haradah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Haradah and camped in Makheloth.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Makheloth and camped at Tahath.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Tarah and camped in Mithkah.
}

\eOther{
	And they went from Mithkah and camped in Hashmonah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Hashmonah and camped at Moseroth.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Moseroth and camped in Bene-jaakan.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Bene-jaakan and camped at
	Hor-haggidgad.
}

\eOther{
	And they went from Hor-haggidgad and camped in Jotbathah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Jotbathah and camped at Ebronah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Ebronah and camped at Ezion-geber.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Ezion-geber and camped in the
	wilderness of Zin. That is Kadesh.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Kadesh and camped in Mount Hor, at
	the edge of the land of Edom.
}

\eOther{
	And Aaron, the priest, went up into Mount Hor at the word
	of YHWH and died there in the fortieth year after the
	children of Israel came out of the land of Egypt, in the
	fifth month, on the first day of the month.
}

\eOther{
	And Aaron was a hundred twenty-three years old when he
	died in Mount Hor.
}

\eOther{
	And the Canaanite, the king of Arad, who lived in the
	Negeb in the land of Canaan, heard of the coming of the
	children of Israel.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Mount Hor and camped in Zalmonah.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Zalmonah and camped in Punon.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Oboth and camped in Iyye-abarim, in
	the border of Moab.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Iyyim and camped in Dibon-gad.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Dibon-gad and camped in
	Almon-diblathaim.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from Almon-diblathaim and camped in the
	mountains of Abarim in front of Nebo.
}

\eOther{
	And they traveled from the mountains of Abarim and camped
	in the plains of Moab by the Jordan toward Jericho.
}

\eOther{
	And they camped by the Jordan from Beth-jeshimoth to
	Abel-shittim in the plains of Moab.
}

\eP{
	And YHWH spoke to Moses in the plains of Moab by the
	Jordan toward Jericho, saying,
}

\eP{
	“Speak to the children of Israel, and you shall say to
	them: When you cross the Jordan to the land of Canaan,
}

\eP{
	you shall dispossess all the residents of the land in
	front of you, and destroy all their carved figures, and
	you shall destroy all their molten images and demolish all
	their high places.
}

\eP{
	And you shall take possession of the land and live in it,
	because I’ve given the land to you to possess it.
}

\eP{
	And if you don’t dispossess the residents of the land in
	front of you, then those whom you leave of them will
	become sticks in your eyes and thorns in your sides, and
	they’ll afflict you on the land in which you’re living.
}

\eP{
	And it will be that, as I meant to do to them, I’ll do to
	you!”
}

\eP{
	“Command the children of Israel, and you shall say to
	them: When you come to the land of Canaan, this is the
	land that will fall to you as a legacy, the land of Canaan
	by its borders:
}

\eP{
	And the southern side for you shall be from the wilderness
	of Zin next to Edom, and the southern border for you shall
	be from the edge of the Dead Sea to the east.
}

\eP{
	And the border for you shall turn from the south to the
	ascent of Akrabim and will pass to Zin, and its extent
	shall be from the south to Kadesh-barnea, and it shall go
	out to Hazar-addar and pass to Azmon.
}

\eP{
	And the border shall turn from Azmon to the Wadi of Egypt,
	and its extent shall be to the sea.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		the wadi of Egypt. This refers to the Wadi el-‘Arîsh.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	And the western border: and the big sea shall be a border
	for you. This shall be the western border for you.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		the big sea. The Mediterranean Sea.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	And this shall be the northern border for you: you shall
	mark from the big sea to Mount Hor,
}

\eP{
	from Mount Hor you shall mark to the entrance of Hamath,
	and the border’s extent shall be to Zedad,
}

\eP{
	and the border shall go out to Ziphron, and its extent
	shall be to Hazar-enan. This shall be the northern border
	for you.
}

\eP{
	And you shall mark for the border to the east from
	Hazar-enan to Shepham,
}

\eP{
	and the border shall go down from Shepham to Riblah at the
	east of Ain, and the border shall go down and rub on the
	shoulder of the Sea of Kinneret on the east,
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		Sea of Kinneret. The Sea of Galilee. Footnote 34:11. shoulder … on the
%		east. On the east side of the Sea of Galilee is a mountain wall, a
%		“shoulder,” known as the Golan Heights.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	and the border shall go down to the Jordan, and its extent
	will be to the Dead Sea. This shall be the land for you by
	its borders all around.”
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		the Dead Sea. In Hebrew it is called “the Salt Sea.”
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	And Moses commanded the children of Israel, saying, “This
	is the land that you shall give as legacies by lot, which
	YHWH commanded to give to the nine tribes and the half of
	a tribe.”
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		nine tribes and the half of a tribe. The half of a tribe is half of the
%		tribe of Manasseh. The other half of Manasseh took land on the east side
%		of the Jordan along with the tribes of Reuben and Gad.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	Because the tribe of the children of the Reubenites by
	their fathers’ house and the tribe of the children of the
	Gadites by their fathers’ house had taken and half of the
	tribe of Manasseh had taken their legacy.
}

\eP{
	The two tribes and the half of a tribe had taken their
	legacy from across the Jordan toward Jericho on the east
	side—to the east.
}

\eP{
	“These are the names of the people who will give the land
	as legacies to you: Eleazar, the priest, and Joshua son of
	Nun;
}

\eP{
	and you shall take one chieftain for each tribe to give
	the land as legacies.
}

\eP{
	And these are the people’s names: For the tribe of Judah,
	Caleb son of Jephunneh.
}

\eP{
	And for the tribe of the children of Simeon, Samuel son of
	Ammihud.
}

\eP{
	And for the tribe of the children of Dan, a chieftain,
	Bukki son of Jogli.
}

\eP{
	For the children of Joseph: for the tribe of the children
	of Manasseh, a chieftain, Hanniel son of Ephod;
}

\eP{
	and for the tribe of the children of Ephraim, a chieftain,
	Kemuel son of Shiphtan.
}

\eP{
	And for the tribe of the children of Zebulun, a chieftain,
	Elizaphan son of Parnach.
}

\eP{
	And for the tribe of the children of Issachar, a
	chieftain, Paltiel son of Azzan.
}

\eP{
	And for the tribe of the children of Asher, a chieftain,
	Ahihud son of Shelomi.
}

\eP{
	And for the tribe of the children of Naphtali, a
	chieftain, Pedahel son of Ammihud.”
}

\eP{
	These are the ones whom YHWH commanded to give the
	children of Israel legacies in the land of Canaan.
}

\eP{
	And YHWH spoke to Moses in the plains of Moab by the
	Jordan toward Jericho, saying,
}

\eP{
	“Command the children of Israel that, from the legacy of
	their possession, they shall give the Levites cities in
	which to live, and you shall give the Levites surrounding
	land for the cities all around them.
}

\eP{
	And the cities shall be theirs to live in, and their
	surrounding lands shall be for their cattle and for their
	property and for their animals.
}

\eP{
	And the surrounding lands of the cities that you shall
	give to the Levites: from the city wall outward, a
	thousand cubits all around.
}

\eP{
	And the cities that you shall give to the Levites: six
	cities of refuge that you shall give for the manslayer to
	flee there, and you shall give in addition to them
	forty-two cities.
}

\eP{
	All the cities that you shall give to the Levites:
	forty-eight cities, them and their surrounding lands.
}

\eP{
	“Speak to the children of Israel, and you shall say to
	them: When you cross the Jordan to the land of Canaan,
}

\eP{
	you shall establish cities; they shall be cities of refuge
	for you, and a manslayer who strikes a life by mistake
	shall flee there.
}

\eP{
	And you shall have the cities for refuge from an avenger
	so the manslayer will not die until he stands in front of
	the congregation for judgment.
}

\eP{
	And the cities that you shall give: You shall have six
	cities of refuge.
}

\eP{
	You shall put three of the cities across the Jordan, and
	you shall put three of the cities in the land of Canaan.
	They shall be cities of refuge.
}

\eP{
	“These six cities shall be for refuge for the children of
	Israel and for the alien and for the visitor among them,
	for anyone who strikes a life by mistake to flee there.
}

\eP{
	But if he struck him with an iron item so that he died, he
	is a murderer. The murderer shall be put to death.
}

\eP{
	And if he struck him with a stone in the hand by which one
	could die, so that he died, he is a murderer. The murderer
	shall be put to death.
}

\eP{
	Or if he struck him with a wooden object in the hand by
	which one could die, so that he died, he is a murderer.
	The murderer shall be put to death.
}

\eP{
	The blood avenger, he shall kill the murderer. When he
	comes upon him, he shall kill him.
}

\eP{
	And if he pushed him in hatred or threw something on him
	through scheming so that he died,
}

\eP{
	or if he struck him with his hand in enmity so that he
	died, the one who struck shall be put to death. He is a
	murderer. The blood avenger shall kill the murderer when
	he comes upon him.
}

\eP{
	But if by chance, not in enmity, he pushed him or threw
	any object on him not through scheming,
}

\eP{
	or with any stone by which one could die, without seeing,
	so that he dropped it on him so that he died, and he was
	not an enemy to him and was not seeking to harm him,
}

\eP{
	then the congregation shall judge between the one who
	struck and the blood avenger on the basis of these
	judgments.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		the death of the high priest. Why does the high priest’s death release
%		him? It makes atonement for the crime. After that, the person who killed
%		by accident is innocent, and if a blood avenger would kill him it would
%		be murder.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	But if the murderer will go out of the border of his city
	of refuge to which he will flee,
}

\eP{
	and the blood avenger will find him outside of the border
	of his city of refuge, and the blood avenger will murder
	the murderer, he does not have blood,
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		he does not have blood. Meaning: he does not have guilt for shedding the
%		blood of the person who killed someone by accident.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	because he shall live in his city of refuge until the high
	priest’s death, and after the high priest’s death the
	murderer shall go back to the land of his possession.
}

\eP{
	“And these shall become a law of judgment for you through
	your generations in all your homes.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		law of judgment. See the comment on Num 27:11.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	Anyone who strikes a life, the murderer shall be murdered
	by the mouth of witnesses. And one witness shall not
	testify against a person so as to die.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		one witness. A person cannot be executed on the testimony of only one
%		witness. There must be two or more.
%	}

tex.english:
\eP{
	And you shall not take a ransom for a murderer’s life,
	because he did wrong so as to die, but he shall be put to
	death.
}

\eP{
	And you shall not take a ransom to flee to his city of
	refuge, to go back to live in the land until the priest’s
	death.
}

\eP{
	So you shall not pollute the land in which you are.
	Because blood: it will pollute the land, and the land will
	not have expiation for blood that is spilled in it except
	by the blood of the one who spilled it!
}

\eP{
	And you shall not make the land impure in which you are
	living, in which I tent, because I, YHWH, tent among the
	children of Israel.”
}

\eP{
	And they said, “YHWH commanded my lord to give the land as
	legacy by lot to the children of Israel, and my lord was
	commanded by YHWH to give the legacy of Zelophehad, our
	brother, to his daughters.
}

\eP{
	And if the children of Israel will have the jubilee, then
	their legacy will be added onto the legacy of the tribe to
	whom they will belong, and their legacy will be subtracted
	from the legacy of our fathers’ tribe.”
}

\eP{
	And Moses commanded the children of Israel by YHWH’s word,
	saying, “The children of Joseph speak right.
}

\eP{
	This is the thing that YHWH has commanded Zelophehad’s
	daughters, saying: They shall become wives for any in
	whose eyes it is good, except: they shall become wives to
	the family of their father’s tribe.
}

\eP{
	So a legacy of the children of Israel will not turn from
	tribe to tribe, but the children of Israel shall each
	cling to the legacy of his fathers’ tribe.
}

\eP{
	And any daughter who inherits a legacy from the tribes of
	the children of Israel shall become a wife to someone from
	a family of her father’s tribe, so that the children of
	Israel will each inherit his fathers’ legacy,
}

\eP{
	and a legacy will not turn from a tribe to another tribe,
	but the tribes of the children of Israel shall each cling
	to its legacy.”
}

\eP{
	As YHWH commanded Moses, so Zelophehad’s daughters did.
}

\eP{
	And Mahlah, Tirzah, and Hoglah and Milcah and Noah,
	Zelophehad’s daughters, became wives to their uncles’
	sons.
}

\eP{
	They became wives within the families of the children of
	Manasseh son of Joseph, and their legacy was on the tribe
	of their father’s family.
}

\eP{
	These are the commandments and the judgments that YHWH
	commanded by Moses’ hand to the children of Israel in the
	plains of Moab by the Jordan toward Jericho.
}

\eDtrA{
	These are the words that Moses spoke to all of Israel
	across the Jordan in the wilderness, in the plain opposite
	Suph between Paran and Tophel and Laban and Hazeroth and
	Di-zahab,
}

\eDtrA{
	eleven days from Horeb by way of Mount Seir up to
	Kadesh-barnea.
}

\eDtrA{
	And it was in the fortieth year, in the eleventh month, on
	the first of the month, Moses spoke to the children of
	Israel of everything that YHWH commanded him to them.
}

\eDtrA{
	After he struck Sihon, king of the Amorites, who lived in
	Heshbon, and Og, king of Bashan, who lived in Ashtaroth at
	Edrei,
}

\eDtrA{
	across the Jordan in the land of Moab, Moses undertook to
	make this instruction clear, saying,
}

\eDtrA{
	“YHWH our God spoke to us in Horeb, saying, ‘You’ve had
	enough of staying at this mountain.
}

\eDtrA{
	See: I’ve put the land in front of you. Come and possess
	the land that YHWH swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to
	Isaac, and to Jacob, to give to them and to their seed
	after them.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And I said to you at that time, saying, ‘I’m not able to
	carry you by myself.
}

\eDtrA{
	YHWH, your God, has made you multiply, and here today
	you’re like the stars of the skies for multitude.
}

\eDtrA{
	(May YHWH, your fathers’ God, add on to you a thousand
	times more like you! And may He bless you as He spoke to
	you.)
}

\eDtrA{
	How shall I carry your stress and your burden and your
	quarrels by myself?
}

\eDtrA{
	Get wise and understanding and knowledgeable people for
	your tribes, and I’ll set them among your heads.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And you answered me, and you said, ‘The thing that you’ve
	spoken is good to do.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And I took heads of your tribes, wise and knowledgeable
	people, and I set them as heads over you, chiefs of
	thousands and chiefs of hundreds and chiefs of fifties and
	chiefs of tens and officers for your tribes.
}

\eDtrA{
	And I commanded your judges at that time, saying, ‘Hear
	between your brothers, and you shall judge with justice
	between a man and his brother or between him and his
	alien.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		recognize a face in judgment. Meaning: you shall not show favoritism to
%		anyone in a legal proceeding.
%	}

tex.english:
\eDtrA{
	And I commanded you at that time all the things that you
	should do.
}

\eDtrA{
	“And we traveled from Horeb and went through all that big
	and fearful wilderness that you’ve seen by way of the
	Amorite hill country as YHWH, our God, commanded us, and
	we came to Kadesh-barnea.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		from Horeb … to Kadesh-barnea. Moses covers the trip from Horeb to the
%		area near the promised land in a single sentence. Thus the text again
%		conveys that the journey could have been a simple thing—eleven days, as
%		in v. 2—but the people’s condition turned it into forty years.
%	}

tex.english:
\eDtrA{
	And I said to you, ‘You’ve come to the Amorite hill
	country that YHWH, our God, is giving us.
}

\eDtrA{
	See: YHWH, our God, has put the land in front of you. Go
	up, possess it as YHWH, your fathers’ God, spoke to you.
	Don’t be afraid and don’t be dismayed.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And you came forward to me, all of you, and said, ‘Let’s
	send men ahead of us, and let them explore the land for us
	and bring us back word of the way by which we’ll go up and
	of the cities to which we’ll come.’
}

\eDtrA{
	And the thing was good in my eyes, and I took twelve men
	from you, one man per tribe.
}

\eDtrA{
	And they turned and went up to the hill country and came
	to the Wadi Eshcol and spied it out.
}

\eDtrA{
	And they took some of the land’s fruit in their hand and
	brought it down to us, and they brought us back word and
	said, the land that YHWH, our God, is giving us is good.
}

\eDtrA{
	But you weren’t willing to go up, and you rebelled against
	the word of YHWH, your God,
}

\eDtrA{
	and you grumbled in your tents and said, ‘Because of
	YHWH’s hatred for us He brought us out from the land of
	Egypt, to put us in the Amorite’s hand to destroy us!
}

\eDtrA{
	To where are we going up? Our brothers have melted our
	heart, saying, “We saw a bigger and taller people than we
	are, big cities and fortified to the skies, and also
	giants!”’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And I said to you, ‘Don’t be scared and don’t be afraid
	of them.
}

\eDtrA{
	YHWH, your God, who is going in front of you, He will
	fight for you—like everything that He did with you in
	Egypt before your eyes
}

\eDtrA{
	and in the wilderness, as you’ve seen that YHWH, your God,
	carried you the way a man would carry his child through
	all the way that you’ve gone until you came to this place.
}

\eDtrA{
	who was going in front of you on the way to scout a
	camping place for you, in fire at night to let you see the
	way in which you would go, and in a cloud by day?!’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And YHWH heard the sound of your words and was angry and
	swore, saying,
}

\eDtrA{
	‘Not a man of these people, this bad generation, will see
	the good land that I swore to give to your fathers;
}

\eDtrA{
	just Caleb son of Jephunneh: he will see it, and I shall
	give the land on which he went to him and to his children
	because he went after YHWH fully.’
}

\eDtrA{
	(YHWH was incensed at me, too, because of you, saying,
	‘You, too, shall not come there.
}

\eDtrA{
	Joshua son of Nun, who is standing in front of you: he
	shall come there. Strengthen him, because he shall get
	Israel its legacy.’)
}

\eDtrA{
	‘And your infants whom you said would become a spoil, and
	your children today who haven’t known good and bad, they
	will come there, and I’ll give it to them, and they will
	possess it.
}

\eDtrA{
	But you: turn and travel to the wilderness by way of the
	Red Sea.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And YHWH said to me, ‘Say to them: You shall not go up,
	and you shall not fight, because I am not among you, so
	you won’t be stricken before your enemies.’
}

\eDtrA{
	And I spoke to you, but you didn’t listen, and you
	rebelled against YHWH’s word and acted presumptuously and
	went up to the hill country.
}

\eDtrA{
	And the Amorite who lives in that hill country came out at
	you and pursued you the way bees do, and they crushed you
	in Seir as far as Hormah.
}

\eDtrA{
	And you came back and wept in front of YHWH, but YHWH
	didn’t listen to your voices and didn’t hear you!
}

\eDtrA{
	“So you lived in Kadesh many days—as many days as you
	lived there—
}

\eDtrA{
	and we turned and traveled to the wilderness by way of
	the Red Sea as YHWH spoke to me, and we stayed around
	Mount Seir many days.
}

\eDtrA{
	‘You’ve had enough of staying around this mountain. Turn
	north.
}

\eDtrA{
	And command the people, saying: You’re crossing the border
	of your brothers, the children of Esau, who live in Seir.
	And they’ll be afraid of you, so be very watchful.
}

\eDtrA{
	Don’t get agitated at them, because I won’t give you any
	of their land, even as much as a footstep, because I’ve
	given Mount Seir to Esau as a possession.
}

\eDtrA{
	Food: you shall buy from them with money, and then you’ll
	eat. And water, too: you shall purchase from them with
	money, and then you’ll drink.
}

\eDtrA{
	Because YHWH, your God, has blessed you in all your hand’s
	work. He has known your walking in this big wilderness.
	These forty years, YHWH, your God, has been with you. You
	haven’t lacked a thing.’
}

\eDtrA{
	So we passed by our brothers, the children of Esau, who
	live in Seir, from the way of the plain, from Eilat, and
	from Ezion-geber, and we turned and passed by way of the
	wilderness of Moab.
}

\eDtrA{
	“And YHWH said to me, ‘Don’t oppose Moab and don’t agitate
	them with war, because I won’t give you a possession from
	its land, because I’ve given Ar as a possession to the
	children of Lot.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		Ar. A Moabite city mentioned in Num 21:15.
%	}

tex.english:
\eDtrA{
	The Emim had lived there before, a people that was big and
	numerous and tall as giants.
}

\eDtrA{
	They were also thought to be Rephaim, like the giants, but
	the Moabites call them Emim.
}

\eDtrA{
	And the Horites lived in Seir before, but the children of
	Esau dispossessed them and destroyed them in front of them
	and lived in their place, as Israel did to the land of its
	possession that YHWH gave them.
}

\eDtrA{
	Now get up and cross the Wadi Zered.’ And we crossed the
	Wadi Zered.
}

\eDtrA{
	And the days that we went from Kadesh-barnea until we
	crossed the Wadi Zered were thirty-eight years, until the
	end of all the generation, the men of war, from among the
	camp, as YHWH swore to them.
}

\eDtrA{
	And YHWH’s hand was against them, to eliminate them from
	among the camp until their end.
}

\eDtrA{
	“And it was when all the men of war had ended, dying from
	among the people,
}

\eDtrA{
	(It, too, was thought to be a land of Rephaim: Rephaim had
	lived there before, and the Ammonites call them Zamzummim,
}

\eDtrA{
	a people that was big and numerous and tall as giants, but
	YHWH destroyed them in front of them, and they
	dispossessed them and lived in their place,
}

\eDtrA{
	as He did for the children of Esau, who live in Seir, in
	that He destroyed the Horite in front of them, and they
	dispossessed them and have lived in their place to this
	day.
}

\eDtrA{
	So the Avvim, who lived in villages as far as Gaza: the
	Caphtorites who left Caphtor destroyed them, and they
	dwelled in their place.)
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		Caphtor. Crete or another of the Greek islands. It is associated with
%		the Philistines (Gen 10:14; Amos 9:7; Jer 47:4; 1 Chr 1:12).
%	}

tex.english:
\eDtrA{
	‘Get up, travel, and cross the Wadi Arnon. See: I’ve put
	Sihon, king of Heshbon, the Amorite, and his land in your
	hand. Begin. Dispossess! And you shall agitate him with
	war.
}

\eDtrA{
	This day I’ll begin to put an awe of you and a fear of you
	on the faces of the peoples under all the skies so that
	when they’ll hear the news of you they’ll tremble and
	writhe in front of you.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And I sent messengers from the wilderness of Kedemoth to
	Sihon, king of Heshbon, words of peace, saying,
}

\eDtrA{
	‘Let me pass through your land. I’ll go on the road, on
	the road! I won’t turn right or left.
}

\eDtrA{
	Food: you’ll sell me for money, and I’ll eat. And water:
	you’ll give me for money, and I’ll drink. Only let me pass
	on my feet
}

\eDtrA{
	as the children of Esau, who live in Seir, and the
	Moabites who live in Ar did for me, until I’ll cross the
	Jordan to the land that YHWH, our God, is giving us.’
}

\eDtrA{
	But Sihon, king of Heshbon, was not willing to let us pass
	through it, because YHWH, your God, had hardened his
	spirit and made his heart bold in order to put him in your
	hand—as it is this day.
}

\eDtrA{
	“And YHWH said to me, ‘See: I’ve begun to put Sihon and
	his land before you. Begin. Dispossess, so as to possess
	his land.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And Sihon came out at us, he and all his people, for war
	at Jahaz.
}

\eDtrA{
	And YHWH, our God, put him before us, and we struck him
	and his sons and all his people.
}

\eDtrA{
	And we captured all his cities at that time, and we put
	every city to complete destruction: men and women and
	infants. We didn’t leave a remnant.
}

\eDtrA{
	Only the animals we despoiled for ourselves, and the spoil
	of the cities that we captured.
}

\eDtrA{
	From Aroer, which is on the edge of the Wadi Arnon and the
	city that is in the wadi, to Gilead, there wasn’t a town
	that was too high for us. YHWH, our God, put it all before
	us.
}

\eDtrA{
	Only to the land of the children of Ammon did you not come
	close, all along the Wadi Jabbok, and the cities of the
	hill country, and whatever YHWH, our God, commanded.
}

\eDtrA{
	“And we turned and went up the way to Bashan. And Og,
	king of Bashan, came out at us, he and all his people, for
	war at Edrei.
}

\eDtrA{
	And YHWH said to me, ‘Don’t be afraid of him, because I’ve
	put him and all his people and his land in your hand, and
	you shall do to him as you did to Sihon, king of the
	Amorites, who lived in Heshbon.’
}

\eDtrA{
	And YHWH, our God, put Og, king of Bashan, and all his
	people in our hand as well, and we struck him until he did
	not have a remnant left.
}

\eDtrA{
	And we captured all his cities at that time. There wasn’t
	a town that we didn’t take from them: sixty cities—all the
	region of Argob, Og’s kingdom in Bashan.
}

\eDtrA{
	All of these were ortified cities—a high wall, double
	gates, and a bar—aside from a great many unwalled cities.
}

\eDtrA{
	And we completely destroyed them as we did to Sihon, king
	of Heshbon, completely destroying every city: men, women,
	and infants.
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		completely destroyed. See the comment on Deut 2:34.
%	}

tex.english:
\eDtrA{
	And we despoiled all the animals and the spoil of the
	cities for ourselves.
}

\eDtrA{
	And at that time we took the land from the hand of the two
	kings of the Amorites that was across the Jordan, from the
	Wadi Arnon to Mount Hermon
}

\eDtrA{
	(Sidonians call Hermon Sirion, and the Amorites call it
	Senir),
}

\eDtrA{
	all the cities of the plain and all of Gilead and all of
	Bashan as far as Salcah and Edrei, cities of Og’s kingdom
	in Bashan.
}

\eDtrA{
	Because only Og, king of Bashan, was left from the rest of
	the Rephaim. Here, his bedstead was a bedstead of iron.
	Isn’t it in Rabbah of the children of Ammon? Its length is
	nine cubits and its width is four cubits by a man’s cubit.
}

\eDtrA{
	And we took possession of this land at that time. I gave
	the Reubenites and the Gadites from Aroer, which is on the
	Wadi Arnon, and half of the hill country of Gilead and its
	cities.
}

\eDtrA{
	And I gave the rest of Gilead and all of Bashan, Og’s
	kingdom, to half of the tribe of Manasseh. All the region
	of Argob: all of that Bashan is called ‘the land of the
	Rephaim.’
}

\eDtrA{
	Jair son of Manasseh had taken all the region of Argob as
	far as the border of the Geshurites nd the Maachathites,
	and he called them, the Bashan, by his name, Havvoth-Jair,
	to this day.
}

\eDtrA{
	And I gave the Reubenites and the Gadites from Gilead to
	the Wadi Arnon, the middle of the wadi being the border,
	and to the Wadi Jabbok, the border of the children of
	Ammon,
}

\eDtrA{
	and the plain, with the Jordan being the border, from the
	Kinneret to the sea of the plain, the Dead Sea, below the
	slopes of Pisgah eastward.
}

\eDtrA{
	“And I commanded you at that time, saying, ‘YHWH, your
	God, has given you this land to take possession of it. You
	shall pass equipped, all the warriors, in front of your
	brothers, the children of Israel.
}

\eDtrA{
	Only your wives and your infants and your livestock (I
	knew that you have a great amount of livestock) shall stay
	in your cities that I’ve given you
}

\eDtrA{
	until YHWH will give your brothers rest like you, and
	they, too, will get possession of the land that YHWH, your
	God, is giving them across the Jordan. Then you shall go
	back, each to his possession that I’ve given you.’
}

\eDtrA{
	And I commanded Joshua at that time, saying, ‘Your eyes,
	that have seen everything that YHWH, your God, has done to
	these two kings: so may YHWH do to all the kingdoms to
	which you’re crossing.
}

\eDtrA{
	You shall not fear them, because YHWH, your God: He is the
	one fighting for you.’
}

\eDtrA{
	‘My Lord, YHWH, you’ve begun to show your servant your
	greatness and your strong hand, for who is a god in the
	skies and in the earth who can do anything like your acts
	and like your victories?!
}

\eDtrA{
	Let me cross and see the good land that’s across the
	Jordan, this good hill country and the Lebanon.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“But YHWH was cross at me for your sakes, and He would not
	listen to me. And YHWH said to me, ‘You have much. Don’t
	go on speaking to me anymore of this thing.
}

\eDtrA{
	Go up to the top of Pisgah and raise your eyes west and
	north and south and east and see it with your eyes,
	because you won’t cross this Jordan.
}

\eDtrA{
	And command Joshua and strengthen him and make him bold,
	because he will cross in front of this people, and he will
	get them the land that you’ll see as a legacy.’
}

\eDtrA{
	“And now, Israel, listen to the laws and to the
	judgments that I’m teaching you to do, so that you’ll
	live, and you’ll come and take possession of the land that
	YHWH, your fathers’ God, is giving you
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		so that you’ll live. This theme of choosing life begins here and will
%		recur several times in the course of Moses’ speech, and culminate in his
%		last sentences (Deut 30:19). See the comment there.
%	}

tex.english:
\eDtrA{
	You shall not add onto the thing that I command you, and
	you shall not subtract from it: observing the commandments
	of YHWH, your God, that I command you.
}

\eDtrA{
	It’s your eyes that saw what YHWH did at Baal Peor, that
	every man who went after Baal Peor: YHWH, your God,
	destroyed him from among you.
}

\eDtrA{
	But you who were clinging to YHWH, your God: you’re all
	alive today!
}

\eDtrA{
	See: I’ve taught you laws and judgments as YHWH, my God,
	commanded me, to do so within the land to which you’re
	coming to take possession of it.
}

\eDtrA{
	And you shall observe and do them because it’s your wisdom
	and your understanding before the eyes of the peoples, in
	that they will hear all these laws and will say, ‘Only a
	wise and understanding people is this great nation.’
}

\eDtrA{
	Because who is a great nation that has gods close to it
	like YHWH, our God, in all our calling to him?
}

\eDtrA{
	And who is a great nation that has just laws and judgments
	like all this instruction that I’m putting in front of you
	today?
}

\eDtrA{
	And you came forward and stood below the mountain, and the
	mountain was burning in fire to the heart of the skies:
	darkness, cloud, and nimbus.
}

\eDtrA{
	And YHWH spoke to you from inside the fire. You were
	hearing the sound of words, but you weren’t seeing a form,
	just sound.
}

\eDtrA{
	And He told you His covenant that He commanded you to do,
	the Ten commandments, and He wrote them on two tablets of
	stones.
}

\eDtrA{
	And YHWH commanded me at that time to teach you laws and
	judgments, for you to do them in the land to which you’re
	crossing to take possession of it.
}

\eDtrA{
	And you shall be very watchful of yourselves—because you
	didn’t see any form in the day that YHWH spoke to you at
	Horeb from inside the fire—
}

\eDtrA{
	in case you’ll be corrupted, and you’ll make a statue, a
	form of any figure, a design of a male or a female,
}

\eDtrA{
	a design of any animal that’s in the earth, a design of
	any winged bird that flies in the skies,
}

\eDtrA{
	a design of anything that creeps on the ground, a design
