tex.english:
\eJ{
	Saul disguised himself; he put on different clothes and set out
	with two men. They came to the woman by night, and he said,
	“Please divine for me by a ghost. Bring up for me the one I shall
	name to you.”
}

tex.commentary:
Qere Ketiv.

\aA{
	Saul puts on a disguise. (Or changes clothes.)
}

\aA{
	They come to the ghost specialist and he says ``Right, I
	need help with a ghost.''
}

tex.original:
\hJ{
	וַתֹּאמֶר הָאִשָּׁה אֵלָיו הִנֵּה אַתָּה יָדַעְתָּ אֵת אֲשֶׁר־עָשָׂה שָׁאוּל אֲשֶׁר הִכְרִית אֶת־הָאֹבוֹת וְאֶת־הַיִּדְּעֹנִי מִן־הָאָרֶץ וְלָמָה אַתָּה מִתְנַקֵּשׁ בְּנַפְשִׁי
	לַהֲמִיתֵנִי׃
}

tex.english:
\eJ{
	But the woman answered him, “You know what Saul has done, how he
	has banned [the use of] ghosts and familiar spirits in the land.
	So why are you laying a trap for me, to get me killed?”
}

tex.commentary:
\aA{
	The woman says ``Alas, Saul has banned the use of
	ghosts, don't talk like that or I could lose my
	license.''
}

tex.english:
\eJ{
	Saul swore to her by YHWH: “As YHWH lives, you won’t get into
	trouble over this.”
}

tex.commentary:
\aA{
	So Saul's like ``Don't worry, I'm cool.''
}

tex.english:
\eJ{
	At that, the woman asked, “Whom shall I bring up for you?” He
	answered, “Bring up Samuel for me.”
}

tex.commentary:
\aA{
	Somehow that works, and she's like ``Ok which ghost?''
}

\aA{
	Saul says ``Samuel.''
}

tex.english:
\eJ{
	Then the woman recognized Samuel, and she shrieked loudly, and
	said to Saul, “Why have you deceived me? You are Saul!”
}

tex.commentary:
\aA{
	It's not clear if she recognized the name Samuel, or if
	she's looking at some kind of ghost menu here. But she
	realizes she's been hoodwinked and it's Saul.
}

tex.english:
\eJ{
	The king answered her, “Don’t be afraid. What do you see?” And the
	woman said to Saul, “I see a divine being coming up from the
	earth.”
}

tex.commentary:
%	\footnote{
%		Footnote 28:13. The woman says she sees gods coming up
%		from the earth. Whatever
%		one thinks happened at Endor, the text lets the dead
%		rise in plural grammar before
%		Samuel speaks in singular doom.
%	}

	\aA{
		So Saul's like ``Get on with it. What do you see?''
	}

	\aA{
		She says ``Something goddy. It's coming out of the
		earth.''
	}

tex.english:
\eJ{
	“What does he look like?” he asked her. “It is an old man coming
	up,” she said, “and he is wrapped in a robe.” Then Saul knew that
	it was Samuel; and he bowed low in homage with his face to the
	ground.
}

tex.commentary:
\aA{
	Saul: Prove it! Tell me what he looks like.
}

\aA{
	Woman: He's old. In a robe!
}

\aA{
	Saul: My god it really is him!
}

tex.original:
\hJ{
